# 103 questions over data/raw, one per document.
#
# How they were made: each question comes from one chunk the index actually
# holds. Most were drafted by the project's own chat model reading that chunk;
# the ones marked las/segy were templated from header fields instead, because a
# model reading one LAS header writes the same question every time.
#
# Every question then had to survive four checks, whatever wrote it:
#   - the answer appears verbatim in the source document
#   - the question does not contain its own answer, or name the file
#   - the question stands alone: no "this well", which nobody could answer
#   - the answer appears in at most 3 documents, so there is one right answer
#
# What this set does not measure: these questions are literal and well-formed,
# because whatever wrote them could see the answer. A person asking vaguely is
# a harder case, and evals/subset.jsonl keeps 22 hand-written questions for it.
#
# By format: docx 1, html 18, las 28, pdf 22, segy 2, shapefile 10, text 22
